  "notes": [
   "The student completes the core (31 units of ECE courses) plus 16 units of General Education (Subtotal 47) and one 6-unit specialization (Total Units: 53). total_units 53 is the certificate total as printed and includes the 16 GE units; GE courses are not placed in a block.",
   "The 16 GE units are for Child Development Permit (Teacher) eligibility: at least one course each in English, Humanities, Social Science, Math/Science. ge_pattern names the catalog's 'General Education Requirements'.",
   "Each specialization (Art with Children, Bilingual/Bicultural Development, Children with Exceptional Needs, Infant and Toddler Care, Music with Children, STEAM in ECE) is one option. Its blocks all carry option_group 'specialization'. Blocks whose names begin with the same specialization name together form one option of 6 units.",
   "Bilingual/Bicultural list also allows 'one foreign language course from French, Spanish or American Sign Language' (no code printed).",
   "Footnote 1: ECE 430 may be used for the Bilingual/Bicultural specialization even if used for the core; the certificate then totals 50 units.",
   "Infant and Toddler Care lists ECE 330 as its choice, though ECE 330 is also a core course; reviewer may wish to verify.",
   "Music with Children: MUFHL 330 or MUIVI 370 (2 units) is printed as an 'or' pair within the 3-unit choice.",
   "ECE 321 and ECE 415 are printed in the core but are not on the closed list (catalog additions).",
   "STEAM in ECE list is split across a repeated table header; both ECE 342 and ECE 361 are read as one 6-unit choice."
  ]
